# H98 (2026-09-13 audit) — no dependency lifecycle scripts, ever.
#
# npm runs every package's preinstall/install/postinstall by default, so `npm ci` in this directory
# used to hand arbitrary code execution to any of the ~4,000 lock lines that arrived with the
# web-ext pin — on the machine that also holds the store credentials and the signing keys. The
# blast radius was the release path itself, at install time rather than test time. This is the
# cheapest control that closes it, and it is per-directory rather than per-command so it also
# covers the contributor path (CONTRIBUTING.md's `npm install`) and the publish runbook's web-ext
# fetch, not just CI.
#
# Nothing in this tree needs a hook: the ONLY `hasInstallScript` package in package-lock.json is
# esbuild, whose postinstall exists to fetch its native binary when the platform-specific
# `@esbuild/<platform>` optional dependency is missing — and the lockfile pins all of them, so the
# hook is a no-op here. If a future dependency genuinely requires one, run its install once,
# deliberately, with `--foreground-scripts --ignore-scripts=false`, and say why in the commit.
#
# Note this does NOT disable this package's own scripts: `npm test`, `npm run build` and
# `npm run package` still run their named script (npm only skips pre-/post- hooks around them,
# and this package.json declares none).
ignore-scripts=true
